  "step_3": "The decision reason requires comparing the probabilities of favorable outcomes and preferring the one with the higher probability. In this case, Lottery B has a 100% chance of a favorable outcome, while Lottery A has a 99% chance (33% + 66%). Therefore, according to the reason, B should be preferred. However, the verbal report does not mention the probability of favorable outcomes at all. Instead, the individual focuses on the marginal gain (100€) and the risk of getting nothing, indicating a risk-averse preference for certainty. The justification does not reflect the rule of the decision reason (preferring higher probability of favorable outcome), even though the outcome differences are negligible. The individual does not evaluate or reference the probability of favorable outcomes. Thus, the decision reason was not used in the deliberation process.",
